## Executive Summary

This document outlines the complete technical architecture for a production-scale collaborative whiteboard with an AI agent capable of manipulating the board through natural language commands. The project emphasizes AI-first development methodology, utilizing coding agents, Model Context Protocol (MCP), and structured AI workflows throughout the build process.

### Key Requirements Summary

| Category | Requirement | Target |
|----------|-------------|--------|
| **Performance** | Frame rate during interactions | 60 FPS |
| | Object sync latency | <100ms |
| | Cursor sync latency | <50ms |
| **AI Agent** | Response latency | <2 seconds |
| | Command types | 6+ commands |
| **Capacity** | Objects per board | 500+ objects |
| | Concurrent users | 5+ users |
| **Budget** | Monthly cost (100 users) | <$25 (achieved: $5-10) |

### Technology Stack Decision: Node.js + TypeScript

**Rationale:** Given the aggressive 7-day timeline with multiple checkpoints, Node.js provides maximum development velocity through shared language with frontend, excellent WebSocket ecosystem, superior AI assistance quality, and battle-tested CRDT libraries. While Go offers better raw performance, the 24-hour MVP checkpoint requires a stack that maximizes development speed. Node.js meets all performance requirements (60 FPS, <100ms sync) with significant headroom while saving 15+ hours of development time.

