## Phase 3: Post-Stack Refinement

### 12. Security Vulnerabilities & Mitigation

| Vulnerability Type | Risk Level | Mitigation Strategy |
|-------------------|------------|---------------------|
| **XSS in AI-Generated Content** | HIGH | DOMPurify sanitization on all AI output before rendering, whitelist safe HTML tags only |
| **WebSocket Authentication Bypass** | HIGH | JWT verification on initial handshake, board access validation per connection, session binding |
| **AI Command Injection** | MEDIUM | Structured prompts with XML boundaries, schema validation on responses, action whitelist enforcement |
| **Rate Limit Denial of Service** | MEDIUM | Express rate limiter (10 AI commands/hour/user), WebSocket cursor throttling (60Hz max) |
| **CORS Misconfiguration** | LOW | Strict origin whitelist (no wildcards), credentials: true for authenticated requests |
| **Dependency Vulnerabilities** | LOW | npm audit in CI/CD, Dependabot alerts, major version pinning, quarterly security reviews |

**Key Points:**
- **Input Validation:** All user input validated against TypeScript schemas using Zod library for runtime type checking
- **Authentication Flow:** Google OAuth → Supabase JWT → httpOnly cookie → WebSocket handshake verification
- **HTTPS Enforcement:** Vercel and Railway enforce HTTPS by default, no HTTP traffic allowed
- **Secret Management:** All API keys and secrets stored in environment variables, never committed to version control
- **Security Headers:** Helmet.js middleware for CSP, XSS protection, clickjacking prevention

